### Hero Entrance Animation — CSS-Driven (Soft Navigation Fix)
- Replaced all Framer Motion `initial={{ opacity: 0 }}` entrance animations in `Hero.tsx` and `Navbar.tsx` with CSS `@keyframes hero-entrance` animations
- CSS animations fire on DOM insertion via browser compositor — no JS chunk dependency
- 6 hero entrance tiers with staggered delays (0s, 0.1s, 0.25s, 0.35s, 0.4s, 0.5s)
- `animation-fill-mode: both` keeps elements invisible during delay, visible after animation
- Navbar no longer has entrance animation — renders immediately for reliability
- `loading.tsx` now shows a visible spinner instead of `null` during soft navigation transitions
- All hero entrance classes respect `prefers-reduced-motion: reduce`

